id: pm-linear-ck8r
title: Drop inert pm manifest key and guard the closed manifest vocabulary
description: "pm-cli's extension-manifest vocabulary is a closed set of 18 keys; since pm-cli 2026.8.19 any other manifest.json key yields a manifest_unknown_key warning. This repo's manifest carried an inert top-level \"pm\": {\"compatibility\": \"v2\"} key that nothing reads, which broke strict-assertion tests downstream (unbraind/pm-linear PRs #75/#76 expected findings exactly ['pm_min_version_unmet'] but got ['manifest_unknown_key','pm_min_version_unmet']). Removed the key, bumped the dev CLI pin from 2026.8.15 to exact 2026.8.22 (the old pin cannot detect unknown keys), and added test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts asserting no manifest_unknown_key findings via checkExtensionManifestCompatibility."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
